{
  "description": "Cross-implementation rendered-stop conformance (ADR-026): composing a stop from the same origin must reach an identical Stop in the Python and TypeScript engines. Each case gives the choices (if any) needed to reach the stop's origin from a fresh read, then the expected composed Stop. 'back_check' cases additionally cover go-back-by-stop (frontend-only; the Python harness only checks the two composed stops independently, since backtracking has no Python-side counterpart, see stops.py's Stop docstring). visit_set is compared as a set (order-independent).",
